The Nautilus DevOps team has some volumes in different regions in their AWS account. 
They are going to setup some automated backups so that all important data can be backed up on regular basis. 
For now they shared some requirements to take a snapshot of one of the volumes they have.

Create a snapshot of an existing volume named datacenter-vol in us-east-1 region using terraform.

1) The name of the snapshot must be datacenter-vol-ss.

2) The description must be Datacenter Snapshot.

3) Make sure the snapshot status is completed before submitting the task.

The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. Update the main.tf file (do not create a separate .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Note: Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
To create the snapshot, you first need to locate the existing volume datacenter-vol using a data source, then create the snapshot from it. 
The key detail is that Terraform's aws_ebs_snapshot resource automatically waits for the snapshot to reach the completed state before finishing .

Here is the content for your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf:
Since the volume already exists in your main.tf as a Terraform-managed resource (not just an existing AWS volume), you should reference it directly by its resource address instead of using a data block. This avoids any lookup issues and keeps a clean dependency chain.

Here is your updated /home/bob/terraform/main.tf:

hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_ebs_volume" "k8s_volume" {
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
  size              = 5
  type              = "gp2"

  tags = {
    Name = "datacenter-vol"
  }
}

resource "aws_ebs_snapshot" "datacenter_snapshot" {
  volume_id   = aws_ebs_volume.k8s_volume.id
  description = "Datacenter Snapshot"

  tags = {
    Name = "datacenter-vol-ss"
  }
}
💡 Why This Works
Direct Reference: aws_ebs_volume.k8s_volume.id refers to the volume already defined in your file, so Terraform knows to create the volume first, then the snapshot.

No Data Source Needed: A data block would fail here because the volume is managed by Terraform in the same configuration — referencing the resource directly is the correct pattern.

Status Wait: aws_ebs_snapshot automatically waits for the snapshot to reach the completed state before Terraform finishes.

🚀 Run
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
✅ Verify (optional)
bash
aws ec2 describe-snapshots \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=datacenter-vol-ss" \
  --query "Snapshots[].{ID:SnapshotId,State:State,Desc:Description,Name:Tags[?Key=='Name']|[0].Value}"
You should see the snapshot with state completed, description Datacenter Snapshot, and name datacenter-vol-ss.
